349	Its ledger is `VERIFY_RESULT_VERSIONS.json`, entries `{ "schema_version", "schemaSha256", "note" }`, newest last, under the same rule as the run-result ledger with `VERIFY_RESULT_SCHEMA_VERSION`. The schema reaches `VerificationEvidence` and `TypecheckEvidence` (`cli/src/core/turn.ts`) and the guard's classes and modes (`cli/src/security.ts`), so a change to any of them needs a regenerated schema and an entry here as well as for the run result. `cli/test/verify_schema.test.ts` runs the comparison, and every result document the `nexus verify` tests produce is validated against the schema. The manual (`docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, "`nexus verify`") describes the document and the exit codes.
